-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Arms): Improved Charge -- flat rage, and a kill reset
-- ============================================================
-- TODO.md: "Improved Charge (0, 1): Increases the amount of rage generated by
--           your Charge ability by 10. Killing an enemy has a 50/100% chance to
--           reset the cooldown on Charge. (2 ranks)"
--
-- The rage bonus becomes flat 10 at BOTH ranks, so the per-rank scaling is
-- entirely the reset chance.  That makes rank 1 a weak purchase relative to
-- rank 2, which is what TODO.md asks for.
--
-- Charge's rage is not an ENERGIZE effect -- it is a SPELL_EFFECT_DUMMY handled
-- in C++, with the amount stored in TENTHS of rage (spell 100 has base points
-- 89 = 9 rage).  Improved Charge modifies it with ADD_FLAT_MODIFIER and
-- EffectMiscValue 8 = SPELLMOD_ALL_EFFECTS, so base points here are also
-- tenths: 99 gives CalcValue 100 = +10 rage.  The stock "$/10;s1" in the
-- description renders that correctly with no edit.
--
-- Prior art for the trigger: PROC_FLAG_KILL (0x2) is stock and widely used --
-- Victorious State 32215, Rapid Killing 34948/34949, Spirit Tap 15270.
--
-- There is NO prior art for the reset, and none is possible:
-- SPELL_EFFECT_RESET_COOLDOWN does not exist in 3.3.5 (it is a Cataclysm
-- effect).  Every cooldown reset in the core is a script -- Preparation,
-- Readiness, Cold Snap.  Hence the small script; see WarriorImprovedCharge.cpp.
--
-- Spells:
--   12285 = Improved Charge Rank 1 (+10 rage, 50% reset)
--   12697 = Improved Charge Rank 2 (+10 rage, 100% reset)
-- ============================================================

-- ============================================================
-- 12285 / 12697
-- ============================================================
-- Effect 1 is untouched apart from base points -- it keeps aura 107, its
-- EffectMiscValue 8 and its EffectSpellClassMaskA1 = 0x1 (Charge), all of which
-- are load-bearing.
--
-- Effect 2 is new: a bare SPELL_AURA_DUMMY that exists only as a hook for the
-- script.  Its class masks are explicitly zeroed rather than left to inherit
-- effect 1's Charge mask.
--
-- The 50/100 lives in ProcChance, not in base points.  The proc system rolls
-- it (spell_proc Chance 0 inherits the DBC value), and $h renders it, so the
-- script needs no knowledge of the number at all.

DELETE FROM `alonecraft_spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (12285, 12697);
